# Loop engineering (mandatory on every prompt)

This repo **always** uses loop engineering. Follow `.cursor/skills/loop-engineering/SKILL.md` on every coding turn. Do not skip it.

Source: [selmakcby/loop-engineering](https://github.com/selmakcby/loop-engineering) (Cursor-adapted).

## Non-negotiable

**Never let the AI verify its own "done."** Maker ≠ checker. "Looks fine" / "should work" is not a gate.

## Required on every coding turn

1. Prefer **Automatic + Closed** when the user says keep going / fix until / run until green.
2. Before claiming code work is finished, run the mechanical gate:
   - `node .cursor/hooks/loop-gate.js`
   - or at least `npm run smoke:subject` when only subject math changed
3. If `main/`, `renderer/`, or `scripts/` JS changed and the gate was not run → **not done**. Keep fixing.
4. Respect the `stop` hook in `.cursor/hooks.json` (`loop_limit: 8`). If the gate is red, continue until green or the ceiling.
5. Docs-only / one-shot Q&A: answer normally — still never invent "tests passed."

## Honesty test (before a long autonomous loop)

Only start a long CreateGoal/`/loop` if work is repetitive, verification is automatable, budget is OK, and tools can run checks. Otherwise use a plain prompt.

## Wiring (do not remove)

| Piece | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Skill (read/follow) | `.cursor/skills/loop-engineering/SKILL.md` |
| Stop gate | `.cursor/hooks/loop-gate.js` |
| Hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` |

CreateGoal / `/loop` only when the user explicitly asks for a goal or interval loop. This always-on rule + stop gate already cover everyday prompts.
